
Usage: /EXEC <script> [arguments]
  EXECute a script that is permitted to you by the system.  Typically,
  you  can  execute  your own and system scripts.  If you are a SysOp,
  you may execute any script by specifying the filename.  You may pass
  arguments to the script if it accepts them.

  The default scripts are:

  Script        Purpose
  -----------   -----------------------------------------------------
  DEFAULT-ENV   Load default environment variables.
  SYS-LOGIN     The  script the system executes before your own login
                script USER-LOGIN.
  SYS-LOGOUT    This script is always executed by the system when you
                /QUIT MTalk.
  USER-ENV      This is your own environment variables script.
                Essentially, /EXEC USER-ENV is same as /SETENV LOAD.
  USER-LOGIN    This script is normally executed when you first enter
                MTalk.
  USER-LOGOUT   This script is normally executed when you /QUIT MTalk
                right after SYS-LOGOUT.

